th] is not prime; ∴[math]x[/math] is divisible by [math]3[/math]\n$$" 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186198123 1074 "The logical inference rule of *disjunctive syllogism* asserts that if $P$ or $Q$ is true, yet $P$ is false, then $Q$ must be true.\n\nLet's denote:\n\n- $D(x)$: $x$ is divisible by $3$\n- $P(x)$: $x$ is prime\n\nThen, using our disjunctive syllogism inference rule, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\nD∨P; ¬P; ∴D\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n$$\nx divisible by 3 or x is prime; x is not prime; ∴x is divisible by 3\n$$" 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186198759 1071 "The notation\n$lim_(n → ∞)\\frac{2}{3n + 1} = 0$\nmeans the following:\n\nFor any real\n{{field-1}} {{field-2}}\nnatural number $N$ such that\n{{field-3}}\nnatural number\n{{field-4}} $$,\nwe have\n$\\mid \\frac{2}{3n + 1} \\mid$ {{field-5}}." 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186198759 1071 "The notation\n$lim_(n → ∞)\\frac{2}{3n + 1} = 0$\nmeans the following:\n\nFor any real\n{{field-1}} {{field-2}}\nnatural number $N$ such that\n{{field-3}}\nnatural number\n{{field-4}} ,\nwe have\n$\\mid \\frac{2}{3n + 1} \\mid$ {{field-5}}." 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186198766 1071 "The notation\n$lim_(n → ∞)\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{n}} = 0$\nmeans the following:\n\n{{field-1}}\nreal $ε > 0$\nthere exists a\n{{field-2}}\nnumber $N$ such that for every\n{{field-3}}\nnumber $n$, if\n{{field-4}} $$,\nthen $\\mid \\frac{5}{\\sqrt{n}} \\mid$ {{field-5}} {{field-6}}." 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186198766 1071 "The notation\n$lim_(n → ∞)\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{n}} = 0$\nmeans the following:\n\n{{field-1}}\nreal $ε > 0$\nthere exists a\n{{field-2}}\nnumber $N$ such that for every\n{{field-3}}\nnumber $n$, if\n{{field-4}} ,\nthen $\\mid \\frac{5}{\\sqrt{n}} \\mid$ {{field-5}} {{field-6}}." 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186198819 1071 "The notation\n$lim_(n → ∞)(3n + 1) = ∞$\nmeans the following:\n\nFor any real\n{{field-1}} {{field-2}}\nnatural number $N$ 