s the price, in dollars, of each marker." 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186208443 1071 "Ella and Noah bought pencils and markers at an art store. The cost of each pencil was the same, as was the cost of each marker. Ella bought $4$ pencils and $5$ markers for $\\[math]19$. In contrast, Noah bought $7$ pencils and $2$ markers for $\\[/math]13$.\n\nDetermine the system of linear equations representing this situation if $x$ is the price, in dollars, of each pencil and $y$ is the price, in dollars, of each marker." 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186208443 1074 "Let's establish the linear equations that model the given situation.\n\n- Ella bought $4$ pencils at $x$ dollars each, and $5$ markers at $y$ dollars each, for a total of $\\$19$. Thus, we have\n$4x + 5y = 19$.\n- Noah bought $7$ pencils at $x$ dollars each, and $2$ markers at $y$ dollars each, for a total of $\\$13$. Hence, we have\n$7x + 2y = 13$.\n\nPutting these equations together, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\left\\{  \\begin{array}{l}4 x + 5 y = 19 \\\\ 7 x + 2 y = 13\\end{array} \\right. }\n$$" 13194139539448 17592186576411 true] [17592186208443 1074 "Let's establish the linear equations that model the given situation.\n\n- Ella bought $4$ pencils at $x$ dollars each, and $5$ markers at $y$ dollars each, for a total of $\\[math]19$. Thus, we have\n$4x + 5y = 19$.\n- Noah bought $7$ pencils at $x$ dollars each, and $2$ markers at $y$ dollars each, for a total of $\\[/math]13$. Hence, we have\n$7x + 2y = 13$.\n\nPutting these equations together, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\left\\{  \\begin{array}{l}4 x + 5 y = 19 \\\\ 7 x + 2 y = 13\\end{array} \\right. }\n$$" 13194139539448 17592186576411 false] [17592186208444 1071 "A bookstore bundled together paperback novels and hardcover reference books for a promotion. Each paperback novel cost $\\$20$, and each hardcover book cost $\\$45$. The store assembled a total of $25$ bundles and the tota